        "original_id": "5cc68503-97f4-504c-b42a-4667b06f12e4",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Bactris, Epigaea, Bactris setulosa\n- Places: Mexico, South America, Central America, the Caribbean\n- Concepts: palm genus, flowering plant genus, species size, elevation range\n\nFacts:\n- Bactris is a genus of spiny palms native to Mexico, South America, Central America, and the Caribbean.\n- Most Bactris species are small trees about 2 meters tall, but some Bactris species are large trees and others are shrubs with subterranean stems.\n- Epigaea is a genus of flowering plants in the Ericaceae and comprises three species.\n- Bactris setulosa is one of the largest species in the genus Bactris and is found at the highest elevations.",
